  "description": {
    "text": "The Japanese Gym deck of Erika, Celadon City's Gym Leader, sold as ポケモンジム第2弾「タマムシシティジム エリカ」 (Pokémon Gym 2: Tamamushi City Gym, Erika) on 25 July 1998 with Lt. Surge's deck, the second pair of six. Its 64 cards are 28 different ones: Erika's own Pokémon, Erika as a holo Trainer, a holo Erika's Vileplume, the Celadon City Gym stadium, new Trainers, and reworded copies of older Trainers that the decks share. The cards carry the Gym series' symbol, as Leader's Stadium's and Challenge from the Darkness's do, but no card number or rarity mark. Leader's Stadium reprinted many of them with a rarity mark, and English players got them in Gym Heroes; the deck was the model for the English Erika theme deck. It came with a rule book, counters and a green Gloom coin."
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"GYM\" symbol, and no rarity mark"
  },
